{
  "name": "Account hiring intelligence: job-board changes to Google Sheets and Slack (ATS Job Changes Feed)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1c7204fb-3964-5fe4-9318-726af80c6eb7",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Account hiring intelligence: job-board changes → Google Sheets history + Slack digest\n\n### How it works\nEvery weekday this workflow runs the ATS Job Changes Feed Actor on Apify for your target accounts (public Greenhouse, Lever or Ashby boards). The Actor remembers the previous run of the same `monitorId` and returns only what changed, a summary per company and free hiring signals.\n\n- **Job changes** (new, changed, reopened, closed) are kept as history in the *Job changes* tab.\n- **Account snapshots** (open roles, new and closed counts, top departments) update one row per company in *Accounts*.\n- **Signals** you care about (new department, new country, leadership hiring…) above a confidence threshold go to *Signals*.\n- One **Slack digest** per run lists new or reopened roles and those signals, grouped by account. Nothing new → no message.\n- Boards that could not be read, and a failed run, are reported to Slack instead of being written.\n\n### Setup\n1. Apify: copy your API token. n8n: create a **Header Auth** credential (Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <token>`) and select it in **Run ATS Job Changes Feed**.\n2. Google Sheets: create a spreadsheet with tabs *Job changes*, *Accounts* and *Signals* (header rows are written automatically), connect your Google credential in the three Sheets nodes.\n3. Slack: create an incoming webhook.\n4. Fill in **Configuration**: companies, spreadsheet URL, webhook URL.\n\n### Customization\nEdit `alertSignalTypes` and `minConfidence` in **Configuration**; change the schedule; use one `monitorId` per watch list. The first run records a baseline and posts nothing; rate signals need about a week of runs. Pay per event on Apify (unchanged jobs are free); `maxTotalChargeUsd` caps each run. Built by AGI Tools, the Actor's publisher.",
        "height": 1060,
        "width": 560
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b7f94170-99c9-5b2c-a710-4915f7e16d10",
      "name": "Section: configure and fetch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Edit **Configuration** only. The Actor call returns every record of the run; a failed call goes to the failure alert.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
